# Actions

Actions let Adafruit IO do something for you when a situation occurs: for example, send an email when a temperature feed goes above a value, publish to another feed every morning, or post to a webhook. An action starts with a **trigger** (new data arriving on a feed that matches a condition, or a time schedule) and then runs a series of blocks that can read feed values, do logic and math, and send an email, SMS, webhook request, or feed value.

Actions are built visually with blocks in the **Actions** editor at [io.adafruit.com](https://io.adafruit.com). Create and edit actions there. The API lets you list, inspect, rename, start/stop, and delete them, and you can also create one by posting an action definition you've copied from an existing action.

<aside class="notice">
The older Actions API (<code>/{username}/actions</code> and <code>/{username}/triggers</code>) is deprecated and is not documented here. Use <code>/{username}/dynamic_actions</code>.
</aside>

### The Action Object

Field | Type | Description
----- | ---- | -----------
id | integer | the action's id, used in the paths below
name | string | the action's name
description | string | a description of the action
run_status | string | `started` (the action runs when triggered), `stopped` (it doesn't), or `alerted` (it was stopped automatically after 5 failed runs in a row)
validation_status | string | `invalidated` (waiting to be checked), `validating`, `valid`, or `invalid`. Only `valid` actions run.
bytecode_validation_errors | array | reasons the action is `invalid`, if any
bytecode | object | the action's definition (see below)
schedules | array | the schedules found in the action's triggers, as cron-style strings
watched_feeds | array | feeds whose new data triggers the action
delay_seconds | integer | seconds the action waits after being triggered before it runs
block_count | integer | number of blocks used, or `-1` if the action isn't valid
heavy_block_count | integer | number of blocks that send something out (feed value, email, SMS, webhook), or `-1` if the action isn't valid
run_count | integer | number of times the action has run
failure_count | integer | number of consecutive failed runs
last_run_at | string | time of the most recent run
last_run_log | string | log from recent runs
last_run_output | object | output from the most recent run
last_check_at | string | time of the most recent trigger check
last_check_log | string | log from recent trigger checks
last_check_output | object | result of the most recent trigger check
created_at | string | creation time
updated_at | string | last update time

The `bytecode` object is the action's definition, saved by the Actions editor. It has a `version`, `settings`, a list of `triggers`, and a list of `expressions` (the blocks that run when a trigger fires). It is meant to be written by the editor, so the easiest way to get a valid one is to read it from an action you built there.

### Limits

* An action can have at most 100 blocks, and at most 20 of them can be "heavy" blocks (set feed value, email, SMS, webhook). Actions over these limits are marked `invalid` and never run.
* An action runs at most once every 5 seconds. Triggers that arrive sooner are skipped.
* A single run is stopped if it takes longer than 10 seconds.
* After 5 failed runs in a row, the action's `run_status` becomes `alerted` and it stops running. Editing its `bytecode` resets this.
* The SMS block is limited to 25 messages per day. The email block requires a verified email address.
* Changing an action's `bytecode` resets it to `stopped` if it was `alerted`, and it must be validated again before it will run.
* Actions publish and read feed data like any other client, so feed data rate limits still apply. See Rate Limiting.

## Get All Actions

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/dynamic_actions</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/dynamic_actions
```

> Response Sample:

```json
[
  {
    "id": 42,
    "name": "High temperature alert",
    "description": "Email me when it gets hot",
    "run_status": "started",
    "validation_status": "valid",
    "bytecode_validation_errors": [],
    "schedules": [],
    "watched_feeds": [],
    "delay_seconds": 0,
    "block_count": 6,
    "heavy_block_count": 1,
    "run_count": 12,
    "failure_count": 0,
    "last_run_at": "2026-10-12T14:03:11.000Z",
    "created_at": "2026-10-01T16:20:44.000Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-12T14:03:11.000Z",
    "bytecode": { "version": "1.0.0-beta.1", "settings": {}, "triggers": [], "expressions": [] }
  }
]
```

An array of your actions, ordered by id. Some fields are trimmed in the sample.

### Path Parameters

Parameter |   Type  |  Required |       Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
username | string | true | a valid username string, must be the user who owns the AIO key



## Get Action

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/dynamic_actions/{id}</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/dynamic_actions/{id}
```

> Response Sample:

```json
{
  "id": 42,
  "name": "High temperature alert",
  "description": "Email me when it gets hot",
  "run_status": "started",
  "validation_status": "valid",
  "bytecode_validation_errors": [],
  "run_count": 12,
  "failure_count": 0,
  "last_run_at": "2026-10-12T14:03:11.000Z",
  "last_run_output": {},
  "bytecode": { "version": "1.0.0-beta.1", "settings": {}, "triggers": [], "expressions": [] }
}
```

A single action, including its definition and the logs from its recent runs. Use this to find out why an action isn't running (check `run_status`, `validation_status`, `bytecode_validation_errors`, and `last_run_log`). Some fields are trimmed in the sample.

### Path Parameters

Parameter |   Type  |  Required |       Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
username | string | true | a valid username string
id | integer | true | the action's id



## Create Action

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-post">POST</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/dynamic_actions</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"dynamic_action": {"name": "My action", "description": "Does a thing"}}' \
  https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/dynamic_actions
```

> Response Sample:

```json
{
  "id": 43,
  "name": "My action",
  "description": "Does a thing",
  "run_status": "stopped",
  "validation_status": "invalidated",
  "bytecode": { "version": "1.0.0-beta.1", "settings": {}, "triggers": [], "expressions": [] }
}
```

Creates an action. New actions are `stopped` until you set `run_status` to `started`. If the request is invalid you'll get a `400` with an `error` array of messages.

The `bytecode` is the Blockly-based definition the Actions editor produces, so building one by hand isn't practical. Create actions in the Actions editor.

### Path Parameters

Parameter |   Type  |  Required |       Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
username | string | true | a valid username string

### Body Parameters

All parameters go inside a `dynamic_action` object.

Parameter |   Type  |  Required |       Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
name | string | false | the action's name
description | string | false | a description of the action
run_status | string | false | `started` or `stopped`
bytecode | object | false | the action's definition: an object with `version`, `settings`, `triggers` and `expressions`. Anything else is rejected.



## Update Action

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-put">PUT</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/dynamic_actions/{id}</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -X PUT -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"dynamic_action": {"run_status": "stopped"}}' \
  https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/dynamic_actions/{id}
```

> Response Sample:

```json
{
  "id": 42,
  "name": "High temperature alert",
  "run_status": "stopped",
  "validation_status": "valid"
}
```

Updates an action and returns it. Send only the fields you want to change. Use it to rename an action, or to start (`"run_status": "started"`) and stop (`"run_status": "stopped"`) it. Changing `bytecode` makes the action `invalidated` until it is checked again (this happens automatically in a moment), and an action only runs once `validation_status` is `valid`. Fields are trimmed in the sample.

### Path Parameters

Parameter |   Type  |  Required |       Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
username | string | true | a valid username string
id | integer | true | the action's id

### Body Parameters

All parameters go inside a `dynamic_action` object.

Parameter |   Type  |  Required |       Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
name | string | false | the action's name
description | string | false | a description of the action
run_status | string | false | `started` or `stopped`
bytecode | object | false | the action's definition, see Create Action



## Delete Action

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-delete">DELETE</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/dynamic_actions/{id}</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -X DELETE -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/dynamic_actions/{id}
```

> Response Sample:

```json
{
  "id": 42,
  "name": "High temperature alert"
}
```

Deletes the action and its run history, and returns the deleted action (trimmed in the sample).

### Path Parameters

Parameter |   Type  |  Required |       Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
username | string | true | a valid username string
id | integer | true | the action's id


